## Purpose

Turn the accepted dashboard direction into one production-verified vertical slice while keeping
local Tool Shed databases authoritative and the hosted service advisory. Preserve the public site's
existing routes and presentation while adding authenticated fleet, project, App Server, and Work
Efficiency views backed by a sanitized reporting API.

## Desired Outcome

An authenticated maintainer can use `https://ts.rookaro.com/dashboard/` to navigate reporting
projects, identify attention and stale state, inspect outcome reconciliation, review App Server
health and bounded failure groups, and understand remedial-work measurements with explicit
coverage. Installed Tool Shed clients enroll only after operator approval and report through a
durable, idempotent, privacy-bounded outbox. The public documentation remains static and compatible,
the production application and PostgreSQL data are recoverable, and the entire outcome chain closes.

## First Useful Boundary

- One nginx gateway, one Django application, one PostgreSQL database, and one authenticated maintainer.
- Public static routes remain public and do not depend on the application.
- Dashboard project tabs are Overview, Current Work, Outcome Reconciliation, and Health.
- Fleet views include attention, App Server health, and Work Efficiency with explicit coverage.
- Instance-initiated enrollment issues one revocable opaque reporter token after approval.
- The local reporter uses a durable outbox, singleton worker, bounded polling, heartbeats, quiescence,
  retry, deduplication, and a periodic safety pass.

